<title>LITHUANIA: Lithuania sells 36-day bills at avg 9.15 pct.</title>
<headline>Lithuania sells 36-day bills at avg 9.15 pct.</headline>
<dateline>VILNIUS 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lithuania sold 50 million litas of 36-day Treasury bills at an average yield of 9.15 percent on Monday, versus an average 9.05 percent at an auction of 34-day paper in early September, the central bank said.</p>
<p> MATURITY   AVG YIELD  (LAST TIME)  MIN/MAX   ISSUE  BID   SOLD</p>
<p> 36-day	9.15	  9.05	8.70/9.99   50   60.676  50</p>
<p>Settlement date for today's auction is October 10, and the paper matures on November 15.</p>
<p>-- Riga Newsroom +371 7 22 66 93</p>
</text>
